\p
\v 17 Mosheh¦61219 and¦61220 Aharon¦61220 took¦61218 those¦61223 men¦61222 whose names¦61226 had¦61225 been¦61225 \add ≈given\add*
\v 18 and¦61228 they¦61232 assembled the¦61235 entire community¦61231 that April. \add ≈For each tribe,\add* they¦61236 recorded¦61236 their¦61236 ancestry¦61236 by \add #clan¦61239\add*, counting¦61242 the¦61242 names¦61243 of¦61244 those men who were twenty¦61245 or over,
\v 19 just¦61250 as¦61250 Yahweh¦61252 had¦61251 commanded¦61251 Mosheh¦61255. \add ≈So¦61256\add* he¦61256 counted¦61256 them¦61256 \add there\add* in¦61257 the¦61257 Sinai¦61258 wilderness¦61257,
\v 20-21 individually counting¦61271 those \add in each tribe below\add* by¦61271 their¦61273 \add #clan¦61268\add*, and only including males¦61276 who¦61282 were twenty¦61278 or older and¦61280 able to fight in battle:
\li1 46,500 men from the¦61286 tribe¦61286 of¦61286 Reuven¦61287,
\li1
\v 22-23 59,300 men from¦61308 the¦61317 tribe¦61317 of¦61317 Shimeon¦61318 \add !(Simeon¦61318)\add*,
\li1
\v 24-25 45,650 men from¦61334 the¦61343 tribe¦61343 of Gad¦61344,
