\c 3
\s1 Aharon's sons
\rem /s1 The Levites; The Sons of Aaron; Levites Appointed for Service; Aaron's Sons
\p
\v 1 \add ≈The following\add* are¦62185 the¦62185 descendants¦62185 of¦62185 Aharon¦62186 \add !(Aaron¦62186)\add* and¦62187 Mosheh¦62187 as on¦62188 the day¦62188 when¦62189 Yahweh¦62190 spoke¦62189 with¦62191 Mosheh¦62193 on¦62194 Mt¦62194. Sinai¦62195:
\v 2 Aharon's¦62201 sons¦62199 were: Nadav¦62204 (the¦62202 oldest¦62202), Avihu¦62205, Eleazar¦62206, and¦62207 Itamar¦62207.\x + \xo 3:2: \xt Num 26:60.\x*
\v 3 They were¦62210 \add all\add* anointed¦62214 as¦62219 priests¦62219 and \add ≈served¦62219 in that role\add*,
\v 4 \add ≈except that\add* Nadav¦62222 and¦62223 Avihu¦62223 died¦62221 \add ≈in¦62224 front¦62224\add* of¦62224 Yahweh¦62225 when¦62226 they¦62226 offered \add ≈unacceptable\add* fire¦62227 to¦62229 \add *him¦62230\add* in¦62231 the¦62231 Sinai¦62232 wilderness¦62231, and¦62233 \add so\add* they had no sons¦62233. \add ≈So¦62238\add* Eleazar¦62239 and¦62240 Itamar¦62240 served¦62238 as¦62238 priests¦62238 \add ≈alongside\add* their¦62245 father¦62245 Aharon¦62244.\x + \xo 3:4: \xt Lev 10:1-2; Num 26:61.\x*
\s1 The Levites as ransom for their sons
