\p
\v 5 Then¦63831 Yahweh¦63832 told¦63831 Mosheh¦63835,
\v 6 “Tell¦63838 the \add ≈Israelis¦63842\add* that when any man¦63843 or¦63844 a¦63846 woman¦63846 \add ≈disobeys God by doing¦63848 any of¦63851 the¦63852 things that humans¦63852 do\add* when they're unfaithful towards¦63855 Yahweh¦63855, then¦63856 that person¦63841 is¦63856 guilty¦63856
\v 7 and¦63860 they¦63860 must¦63860 confess¦63860 their¦63863 \add ≈disobedience\add*. Then that¦63864 person must make full reparation to whoever they¦63865 wronged, along with an extra twenty¦63871 percent¦63872 \add of the cost\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈However,\add* if¦63879 reparation to¦63884 \add ≈the¦63885 victim isn't¦63881 possible\add* \add for some reason\add*, then it¦63886 must be¦63888 paid to¦63889 Yahweh¦63889 via a priest¦63890, in addition¦63891 to the¦63892 ram¦63892 \add that will be offered\add* for that¦63894 person's¦63882 atonement¦63895.
\v 9 Any¦63903 sacred¦63905 \add #contributions¦63902\add* by the¦63906 \add ≈Israelis¦63908\add* that¦63909 are presented¦63911 to¦63912 a priest¦63912 will¦63914 belong¦63914 to him.
\v 10 Each person's sacred¦63919 contributions will be their own, \add but\add* anything given¦63925 to¦63926 a priest¦63926 will belong to him.”
\s1 Testing for an unfaithful wife
\rem /s1 Concerning an Unfaithful Wife; Cases of Wives with Suspicious Husbands; Protecting Marital Faithfulness; The Test for an Unfaithful Wife
\p
\v 11 Then¦63931 Yahweh¦63932 told¦63931 Mosheh¦63935,
\v 12 “Tell¦63938 the¦63941 \add ≈Israelis¦63942\add* that if¦63947 any man's wife¦63950 \add ≈has an affair\add* and¦63951 is unfaithful¦63951 towards him¦63952,
\v 13 when¦63955 another man¦63956 secretly has¦63966 sex with her, then she becomes ‘unclean¦63966’, even though there's¦63968 no witness¦63967 against her¦63969 and¦63970 she wasn't¦63968 caught¦63972.
\v 14 \add ≈If the husband becomes suspicious, whether or¦63985 not¦63997 she's¦63998 actually\add* become ‘unclean¦63998’,
\v 15 then¦64000 \add *he\add* should take¦64000 \add *her\add* to¦64005 a priest¦64007. He¦64008 must¦64008 also bring¦64008 an offering¦64011 on her¦64011 behalf: two litres of¦64013 barley¦64016 flour¦64015. It must not have any oil¦64021 or \add ≈spices mixed into it¦64025\add* because¦64027 it's¦64031 a¦64032 grain¦64032 offering¦64032 for suspicion—\add ≈for determining if unfaithfulness has occurred\add*.
\p
\v 16 Then¦64037 the¦64039 priest¦64039 must¦64040 \add ≈lead her¦64040 forward\add* and stand¦64040 her in¦64041 front¦64041 of¦64041 Yahweh¦64042.
\v 17 He¦64044 must¦64044 \add ≈fill\add* a pottery jar with sacred¦64047 water, and¦64051 then mix some dust¦64053 from the¦64056 floor¦64056 of¦64056 \add &Yahweh's¦64057\add* residence¦64057 into¦64061 the¦64063 water¦64063.
\v 18 Then¦64065 the¦64066 priest¦64066 must stand¦64065 the¦64069 woman¦64069 \add ≈in¦64070 front¦64070\add* of¦64070 Yahweh¦64071 and¦64072 \add ≈let¦64072 her hair down\add*, then¦64077 he¦64077 must place the¦64082 suspicion grain¦64082 offering¦64082 on her \add #palm¦64080\add*. (It's a¦64084 grain¦64084 offering¦64084 for jealousy¦64085.) The¦64088 priest¦64088 must be \add ≈holding\add* the¦64090 \add #water¦64090\add* of \add ≈bitterness¦64091\add* that¦64092 brings¦64092 a¦64092 curse¦64092
\v 19 and¦64097 tell¦64097 the¦64100 woman¦64100 to make¦64094 this oath¦64094: “If¦64101 no \add other\add* man¦64105 \add ≈slept\add* with¦64106 you¦64106, and¦64107 if¦64107 you didn't¦64109 \add ≈dirty yourself while you're¦64110 married\add*, then be¦64114 free¦64114 from¦64115 this \add #water¦64115\add* of¦64115 \add ≈bitterness¦64116\add* that¦64117 brings¦64117 a¦64117 curse¦64117.
\v 20 \add ≈But¦64120\add* if¦64121 you¦64122 \add ≈have¦64122 cheated on\add* your¦64124 husband¦64124 and¦64125 become ‘unclean¦64126’ and¦64127 slept with some other guy, \add there'll be consequences\add*.
\v 21 Then¦64136 the priest will make the¦64140 woman¦64140 take that curse as an oath, and¦64143 \add *he'll\add* tell¦64143 \add *her\add*, “Yahweh¦64147 will \add ≈make¦64146 your experience\add* a¦64149 curse¦64149 and¦64150 your¦64152 people¦64152 \add ≈will see the results of¦64152 the\add* oath, when¦64153 Yahweh¦64154 gives \add ≈disease to your genitals\add* and makes¦64153 your¦64157 belly¦64161 swell¦64162.
\v 22 This \add #water¦64165\add* will¦64164 \add ≈invoke\add* the¦64165 curse¦64166 to¦64169 make \add &your¦64170\add* belly¦64170 swell¦64169 and¦64171 your \add ≈genitals shrivel\add*.” Then¦64173 the¦64174 woman¦64174 must say¦64173, “Indeed, let it be so.”
\p
\v 23 Then¦64179 the¦64184 priest¦64184 must¦64179 write¦64179 those¦64183 curses¦64182 on¦64185 a scroll¦64185, then¦64186 wipe¦64186 \add the ink\add* into¦64187 the¦64189 \add #water¦64189\add* of¦64189 \add ≈bitterness¦64190\add*.
\v 24 He must make the¦64195 woman¦64195 drink that water¦64198 of¦64198 \add ≈bitterness¦64199\add* that¦64200 brings¦64200 the curse¦64200, and¦64201 \add *it\add* will¦64201 enter into¦64202 her¦64202.
\v 25 Then¦64207 he'll¦64207 take¦64207 the grain¦64212 offering¦64212 of¦64212 suspicion from her hand¦64209, and¦64214 hold it up \add ≈in¦64218 front¦64218\add* of¦64218 Yahweh¦64219, and¦64220 then take¦64220 it¦64221 to¦64222 the¦64224 altar¦64224.
\v 26 \add *He'll\add* take¦64226 some of the¦64230 grain¦64230 as a memorial¦64233 portion and¦64234 burn¦64234 it on the¦64235 altar¦64235. Then¦64236 he'll¦64237 make¦64237 the¦64240 woman¦64240 drink¦64237 the¦64243 \add #water¦64243\add*.
\v 27 \add ≈After she's¦64249 drunk¦64245 it\add*, if¦64250 she¦64252 was ‘unclean¦64252’ and¦64253 unfaithful to her¦64255 husband¦64255, the¦64258 water¦64258 will carry that¦64259 curse¦64259 into¦64260 her, and¦64261 her¦64262 belly¦64262 will¦64261 swell¦64261 and¦64263 her¦64264 \add ≈genitals will¦64265 get¦64265 diseased\add*, and the¦64266 woman¦64266 will become¦64265 a¦64267 curse¦64267 among¦64268 her¦64269 people¦64269.
\v 28 \add ≈However,\add* if¦64271 she¦64274 hadn't defiled¦64274 herself¦64274 and¦64276 is¦64276 pure¦64276, then¦64278 she'll¦64278 be¦64278 free¦64278 and¦64279 \add be able to\add* \add ≈have children\add*.
\p
\v 29 That's¦64285 the¦64283 rule about¦64283 jealousy¦64284 when a¦64287 wife¦64287 \add ≈cheats on\add* her¦64289 husband¦64289 and¦64290 defiles¦64290 herself¦64290,
\v 30 or¦64292 when a \add ≈husband\add* \add ≈becomes jealous¦64298 and¦64299 suspicious\add* and¦64303 he¦64303 stands¦64303 \add ≈his wife¦64306\add* \add ≈in¦64307 front¦64307\add* of¦64307 Yahweh¦64308, and¦64309 the¦64311 priest¦64311 applies this¦64316 ruling to her.
\v 31 Then¦64318 \add ≈the husband\add* will¦64318 be¦64318 \add ≈innocent\add*, and¦64321 that¦64322 women¦64321 will¦64323 \add ≈bear¦64323 the consequences\add* of¦64326 her¦64326 wrongdoing.
\c 6
\s1 Instructions for the Nazirite vow
\rem /s1 The Nazirites; The Nazirite; Nazirite Laws; Rules for Nazirites
\p
\v 1 Then¦64329 Yahweh¦64330 told¦64329 Mosheh¦64333,
\v 2 “Tell¦64336 the¦64339 \add ≈Israelis¦64340\add* that when¦64341 any man¦64343 or¦64344 woman¦64346 wants to make¦64348 a¦64350 solemn vow¦64350 to¦64352 separate themself to¦64353 Yahweh¦64353 as a Nazirite,
\v 3 they must¦64357 keep¦64357 away from¦64355 wine¦64355 and¦64356 strong¦64356 drink¦64356, and \add even\add* vinegar made from wine or strong¦64361 drink, plus¦64364 they mustn't drink¦64369 grape¦64370 juice¦64366 or eat¦64374 either grapes or raisins.\x + \xo 6:3: \xt Luk 1:15.\x*
\v 4 For the¦64377 entire time¦64377 of¦64377 their separation¦64378, they mustn't eat¦64389 anything coming from a grapevine¦64382, \add ≈not even\add* the¦64383 seeds¦64384 or the \add #skins¦64387\add*.
\p
\v 5 “For the¦64393 entire¦64391 time¦64393 of¦64393 their vow¦64394 to¦64410 Yahweh¦64410 as a Nazirite, they mustn't cut their hair—they must sacred¦64411 and grow¦64413 their hair¦64415 long.
\p
\v 6 “For the¦64420 entire¦64418 time¦64420 of¦64420 their separation to¦64422 Yahweh¦64422, they mustn't approach any dead¦64426 body¦64425,
\v 7 even if it's their father¦64430 or mother¦64431, or brother¦64432 or sister¦64433. They mustn't defile¦64436 themselves with death¦64438, because¦64439 their consecration¦64440 to their god¦64441 is¦64442 on¦64442 their head¦64444.
\v 8 They must remain holy¦64449 to¦64451 Yahweh¦64451 for the whole¦64446 time¦64447.
\p
\v 9 “\add ≈However,\add* if someone right next to them suddenly¦64459 died¦64455, that would¦64460 defile¦64460 their \add ≈consecrated¦64462\add* head¦64461, and¦64463 after the \add regular\add* seven days¦64465 of purification¦64466, they would¦64469 have to shave¦64469 their head.
\v 10 Then¦64471 on¦64471 the¦64472 eighth¦64472 day¦64471, they'd have to take¦64473 two¦64474 doves¦64479 or¦64476 young¦64478 pigeons to¦64480 the¦64482 priest¦64482 at the¦64485 entrance¦64485 of¦64485 the¦64486 \add ≈sacred tent¦64486\add*,
\v 11 and¦64489 \add *he\add* would¦64489 take one¦64491 for a¦64492 sin¦64492 offering¦64492 and¦64493 the other for a¦64494 burnt¦64494 offering¦64494—making¦64495 atonement¦64495 for¦64497 their transgression with the¦64501 corpse¦64501. Then¦64502 they would¦64502 consecrate¦64502 their head¦64505 \add again\add* that¦64507 day¦64506
\v 12 and¦64509 \add ≈restart\add* their days¦64513 of¦64513 separation¦64514, as well as bringing¦64515 a¦64516 one-year old male lamb¦64516 as a¦64520 guilt¦64520 offering¦64520. (Their initial days¦64521 of separation \add ≈won't count\add* because¦64524 they were made ‘unclean¦64525’.)
\p
\v 13 “Now these are¦64529 the¦64529 instructions¦64529 for the¦64530 Nazirites¦64530: Once their days¦64533 of¦64533 separation¦64534 are fulfilled, \add someone\add* must¦64535 take¦64535 them to¦64537 the¦64539 entrance¦64539 of¦64539 the¦64540 \add ≈sacred tent¦64540\add*
\v 14 and¦64543 they will¦64543 present their offerings¦64546 to¦64547 Yahweh¦64547—an unblemished, one-year old, male lamb as a¦64554 burnt¦64554 offering¦64554, and¦64555 an unblemished¦64560, one-year old, female lamb as a¦64561 sin¦64561 offering¦64561, plus¦64562 an unblemished ram¦64562 as a¦64566 peace¦64566/fellowship offering¦64566,
\v 15 \add ≈along with\add* a¦64568 basket¦64568 of¦64568 flat¦64569 breads¦64569, flour¦64570 mixed¦64572 with¦64573 oil¦64573, and¦64574 wafers¦64574 spread with¦64577 \add olive\add* oil¦64577, and¦64578 their¦64578 grain¦64578 and¦64579 drink¦64579 offerings¦64579.
\v 16 The¦64582 priest¦64582 must present all that to¦64583 Yahweh¦64584, and¦64585 \add ≈handle\add* their sin¦64588 offering and burnt¦64591 offering.
\v 17 The¦64595 ram¦64595 and the¦64601 basket¦64601 of¦64601 flat¦64602 breads¦64602 will¦64596 be offered¦64596 as a¦64597 peace¦64598 offering¦64598 to¦64599 Yahweh¦64599, and¦64603 the¦64604 priest¦64604 will offer¦64607 their grain and¦64608 wine offerings¦64610.
\v 18 Then¦64612 the¦64613 Nazirite¦64613 must shave¦64612 their head of separation at the¦64614 opening¦64614 to the¦64615 \add ≈sacred tent¦64615\add*, and¦64621 taking¦64621 the¦64624 hair¦64624, must put it¦64627 on¦64628 the¦64630 fire¦64630 under¦64633 \add &their\add* peace¦64635 \add #offering¦64635\add* sacrifice¦64634.
\p
\v 19 “The¦64638 priest¦64638 will then take¦64637 the boiled¦64642 shoulder¦64641 from¦64643 the¦64645 ram¦64645, and¦64646 one flat¦64647 bread¦64647 roll and one¦64648 wafer¦64652 from¦64649 the¦64651 basket¦64651, and¦64655 place them on¦64656 the¦64658 palms¦64658 of¦64658 that Nazirite¦64659 with their \add ≈consecrated¦64664\add* head that's been shaved¦64661.
\v 20 Then¦64666 the priest will¦64666 raise them¦64667 as a¦64670 raised offering to¦64671 Yahweh¦64672. Those raised breads and the shoulder \add ≈are¦64673 now sacred¦64673 and¦64679 belong to\add* the priest. Then¦64682 the¦64684 Nazirite¦64684 can drink¦64683 some wine¦64685.
\p
\v 21 Those are¦64688 the¦64688 instructions¦64688 for the¦64689 Nazirite¦64689 who¦64690 \add ≈makes a solemn oath\add* to¦64693 Yahweh¦64693 for their separation¦64696, \add ≈plus what they're able to¦64702 give\add*. \add ≈They must do¦64707 exactly what they promised\add* as per these instructions¦64709.”
\s1 The priests' prayer for blessing
\rem /s1 The Priestly Benediction; The Priestly Blessing
\p
\v 22 Then¦64713 Yahweh¦64714 told¦64713 Mosheh¦64717 \add !(Moses¦64717)\add*,
\v 23 “Tell¦64720 Aharon¦64723 \add !(Aaron¦64723)\add* and¦64724 his¦64726 sons¦64726 that when the bless¦64729 the¦64732 \add ≈Israelis¦64733\add*, this is what they must say¦64734:
\q1
\v 24 May¦64738 Yahweh¦64739 bless¦64738 you¦64738 and¦64740 protect you¦64740.
\q1
\v 25 May \add ≈Yahweh¦64744 give you¦64747 prosperity and¦64748 show¦64748 grace toward\add* you¦64748.
\q1
\v 26 May \add *he\add* \add ≈watch over\add* you¦64755 and¦64756 give you peace¦64758.
\p
\v 27 “\add ≈In that way,\add* they'll¦64761 put¦64761 my¦64764 name¦64764 on¦64765 the¦64767 \add ≈Israelis¦64768\add*, and¦64769 I will¦64770 bless¦64770 them¦64770.”
\c 7
\s1 The leaders' offerings at the altar dedication
\rem /s1 Offerings of the Leaders; The Offerings of the Leaders; Offerings of Dedication; Offerings at the Dedication of the Tabernacle
\p
\v 1 When¦64773 Mosheh¦64776 \add !(Moses¦64776)\add* had finished¦64775 setting¦64777 up¦64777 the¦64780 \add ≈sacred¦64780 tent¦64780\add*, he¦64781 anointed¦64781 it¦64782 \add with oil\add* and¦64783 consecrated¦64783 it¦64784 and¦64785 all¦64787 its¦64789 furniture, as well as the¦64792 altar¦64792 and¦64793 all¦64795 its¦64797 equipment.
\v 2 Then¦64802 Yisrael's¦64804 leaders¦64803 presented¦64802 \add <gifts\add*. They¦64808 were¦64809 the¦64809 leaders¦64809 of¦64809 the¦64810 tribes¦64810 who¦64812 ruled over¦64813 those who'd been listed¦64815 \add for duties\add*.
\v 3 They¦64817 brought¦64817 their¦64820 gifts to¦64821 Yahweh's¦64822 \add ≈presence\add* in six¦64823 carts¦64825 \add pulled by\add* twelve bulls¦64829. Each cart¦64830 was from two¦64833 leaders¦64834, and each of¦64839 the¦64840 bulls was from one¦64836 leader.
\v 4 Then¦64842 Yahweh¦64844 told Mosheh¦64847:
\v 5 “\add ≈Accept¦64850 their gifts because they'll¦64852 be¦64852 useful for the¦64856 running of¦64856 the¦64857 sacred tent¦64857\add*. \add ≈Distribute them¦64860 appropriately to¦64861 the¦64863 Levites¦64863, depending on each¦64864 man's¦64864 duties\add*.”
\v 6 \add ≈So¦64868\add* Mosheh¦64869 took¦64868 the¦64872 carts¦64872 and¦64873 the¦64875 cattle¦64875 and¦64876 distributed them¦64877 to¦64878 the¦64880 Levites¦64880,
\v 7 giving¦64889 two¦64884 carts¦64885 and¦64886 four¦64887 bulls¦64888 to¦64890 the¦64890 Gershonites to¦64892 help¦64893 them with their¦64893 assigned duties.
\v 8 Then¦64895 he¦64902 gave¦64902 four¦64897 carts¦64898 and¦64899 eight¦64900 bulls¦64901 to¦64903 the¦64903 Merarites to¦64905 help¦64906 them with their¦64906 assigned duties under the¦64907 supervision of¦64907 the¦64909 priest¦64912 (Aharon's¦64911 son¦64909) Itamar¦64908.
\v 9 \add ≈However,\add* the¦64914 Kohaties weren't given¦64917 any because¦64918 they were responsible for carrying the \add very\add* holy¦64921 objects, and those had to be¦64922 carried¦64924 on \add &their\add* \add #shoulders¦64923\add*.
\p
\v 10 The¦64927 day¦64931 that the¦64930 altar¦64930 \add ≈was¦64932 dedicated¦64929\add* and anointed¦64932, the¦64935 leaders¦64935 brought their¦64938 gifts and presented them at the¦64940 altar¦64940,
\v 11 and¦64942 Yahweh¦64943 told¦64942 Mosheh¦64946, “\add ≈Each day\add* \add for the next twelve days\add*, one leader must¦64953 present his offering¦64956 for¦64957 the¦64958 altar¦64958 dedication¦64957.”
\p
\v 12-83 \add ≈These were¦64961 the¦64962 leaders who¦64962 presented¦64962 their offerings:\add*
\li1 On the¦64964 first¦64964 day, Amminadav's son Nahshon \add on behalf of\add* the¦64972 tribe¦64972 of¦64972 Yehudah¦64973,
\li1 on the¦65048 second¦65048 day, Zuar's¦65053 son¦65100 Netanel¦65126 \add on behalf of\add* the¦65127 tribe of¦65127 Yissakar¦65055,
\li1 on the¦65133 third¦65133 day, Helon's¦65140 son¦65182 Eliav¦65208 \add on behalf of\add* the¦65209 tribe of¦65209 Zevulun¦65136,
\li1 on the¦65215 fourth¦65215 day, Shedeyur's¦65222 son¦65264 Elitsur¦65290 \add on behalf of\add* the¦65291 tribe of¦65291 Reuven¦65218,
\li1 on the¦65297 fifth¦65297 day, Tsurishaddai's¦65304 son¦65346 Shelumiel¦65372 \add on behalf of\add* the¦65373 tribe of¦65373 Shimeon¦65300,
\li1 on the¦65379 sixth¦65379 day, Deuel's¦65386 son¦65428 Elyasaf¦65454 \add on behalf of\add* the¦65455 tribe of¦65455 Gad¦65382,
\li1 on the¦65461 seventh¦65461 day, Ammihud's¦65468 son¦65510 Elishama¦65536 \add on behalf of\add* the¦65537 tribe of¦65537 Efrayim¦65464,
\li1 on the¦65543 eighth¦65543 day, Pedahzur's son Gamaliel¦65620 \add on behalf of\add* the¦65621 tribe of¦65621 Menashsheh¦65546,
\li1 on the¦65629 ninth¦65629 day, Gideoni's son Avidan \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Benyamin¦65632,
\li1 on the¦65711 tenth¦65711 day, Ammishaddai's¦65718 son¦65760 Ahiezer¦65786 \add on behalf of\add* the¦65787 tribe of¦65787 Dan¦65714,
\li1 on¦65792 the¦65793 eleventh day¦65795, Okran's¦65802 son¦65844 Pagiel¦65870 \add on behalf of\add* the¦65871 tribe of¦65871 Asher¦65798,
\li1 and on¦65876 the¦65877 twelfth day¦65879, Enam's son Ahira \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of¦65882 Naftali¦65882.
\p \add ≈Each of the leaders presented the following offerings¦65888:\add*
\li1 a¦65889 silver dish (1.5 kg—\add ≈all weights\add* by the standard temple measurement) and¦65894 a¦65896 silver bowl (800g)—both¦65903 of¦65903 them¦65903 full¦65905 of fine¦65906 flour¦65906 mixed¦65907 with¦65908 oil¦65908 as a¦65909 grain¦65909 offering¦65909,
\li1 a¦65911 small gold¦65914 dish (110g) filled with incense¦65916,
\li1 a¦65918 young¦65918 bull¦65918, a¦65923 ram¦65923 and a¦65925 one-year-old male lamb¦65925 for a¦65931 burnt¦65931 offering¦65931,
\li1 a¦65933 male¦65933 goat¦65933 for a¦65937 sin¦65937 offering¦65937,
\li1 two¦65942 cows, five rams¦65943, five¦65944 male goats¦65945, and five one-year-old rams for the¦65953 peace offering¦65953.
\p
\v 84 That¦65960 was¦65962 the¦65962 dedication¦65962 of¦65962 the¦65963 altar¦65963 in¦65964 the day¦65964 it was¦65965 anointed¦65965, when Yisrael's¦65969 leaders¦65968 \add presented\add* twelve silver dishes¦65970, twelve silver¦65971 bowls¦65974, and twelve gold¦65980 pans¦65979.
\v 85 Each silver dish¦65986 weighed 1.5kg (\add ≈all¦65992 weights\add* by the¦65987 standard temple measurement) and¦65989 the¦65990 silver bowls¦65990 were 800g. The¦65991 total¦65992 weight of¦65992 the¦65993 silver¦65993 was¦65995 around¦65999 27 kg.
\v 86 The¦66002 gold pans that had been¦66007 filled with incense¦66008 weighed 110g and¦66019 their total¦66014 weight came to 1.3kg.
\v 87 For the¦66023 burnt offerings¦66024 there was¦66025: twelve bulls¦66027, twelve rams¦66028, and twelve male one-year-old lambs¦66032 along with their¦66038 grain¦66038 offerings¦66038. There were twelve male¦66039 goats for¦66043 a¦66043 sin¦66043 offering¦66043.
\v 88 For the¦66049 peace¦66049 offering¦66049, there were¦66050 24 bulls¦66052, 60 rams¦66053, 60 male goats¦66055, 60 male one-year-old lambs¦66057. All¦66045 of¦66058 those were¦66063 part of the¦66063 dedication¦66063 offerings for the¦66064 altar¦66064 after¦66065 it was¦66066 anointed¦66066.
\v 89 Then¦66069 Mosheh¦66070 entered the¦66073 \add ≈sacred tent¦66073\add* to¦66075 speak¦66075 with¦66076 \add @Yahweh¦66076\add*. He¦66077 heard¦66077 the¦66080 voice¦66080 speaking¦66081 to¦66082 him¦66082 from¦66083 between¦66090 the¦66084 two¦66091 images of winged-creatures that¦66085 were¦66086 on¦66086 the platform above the \add sacred\add* box¦66088. That's how \add @Yahweh¦66093\add* spoke¦66093 to¦66094 him¦66094.
\c 8
\s1 Lighting the seven lamps
\rem /s1 The Seven Lamps; Setting Up the Lamps; Placing the Lamps; Preparing the Lamps
\p
\v 1 Then¦66097 Yahweh¦66098 told¦66097 Mosheh¦66101 \add !(Moses¦66101)\add*,\x + \xo 8:1-4: \xt Exo 25:31-40; 37:17-24.\x*
\v 2 “Tell¦66104 Aharon¦66107 \add !(Aaron¦66107)\add* that when¦66110 \add %he¦66110\add* \add ≈places\add* the¦66113 seven¦66120 lamps¦66113 \add on\add* the¦66118 lampstand¦66118, \add ≈they¦66119 must¦66119 light¦66119 up¦66110 the¦66116 area in front¦66116 of¦66117 it\add*.”
\v 3 \add ≈So¦66124\add* Aharon¦66125 did it just¦66133 as¦66133 Yahweh¦66135 had¦66134 instructed¦66134, setting up¦66131 the lamps¦66132 on the¦66130 lampstand¦66130 to face¦66129 forwards.
\v 4 The lampstand from the base¦66147 to¦66148 its¦66150 \add #blossoms¦66150\add* had been¦66151 made¦66161 by hammering¦66151 \add a single sheet\add* of gold¦66144, just¦66140 as¦66153 Yahweh¦66156 had¦66155 shown¦66155 Mosheh¦66159.
\s1 The dedication of Levites
\rem /s1 Consecration and Service of the Levites; The Setting Apart of the Levites; The Purification and Dedication of the Levites; The Levites Dedicated
\p
\v 5 Then¦66167 Yahweh¦66168 told¦66167 Mosheh¦66171,
\v 6 “\add ≈Out of¦66178 all the¦66179 Israelis¦66180\add*, take¦66174 the¦66177 Levites¦66177 and¦66181 purify¦66181 them¦66182.
\v 7 This is how to make¦66193 them pure: sprinkle¦66189 the sin¦66192 offering¦66192 water¦66191 on them, then¦66193 they¦66193 must¦66193 shave their \add ≈entire¦66197 bodies¦66199\add* and¦66200 wash¦66200 themselves and their¦66201 clothes¦66201.
\v 8 They¦66204 must¦66204 take¦66204 a¦66205 \add ≈young¦66205\add* bull¦66205 along with its¦66209 grain¦66209 offering of flour¦66210 mixed¦66211 with¦66212 oil¦66212, plus¦66213 a¦66213 \add ≈second¦66215 young¦66216\add* bull for a¦66220 sin¦66220 offering¦66220.
\v 9 You¦66222 must¦66222 have the¦66225 Levites¦66225 stand at the¦66226 front¦66226 of¦66226 the¦66227 \add ≈sacred tent¦66227\add* and¦66229 summon the¦66234 rest of¦66234 the¦66235 \add ≈Israelis¦66236\add* \add there too\add*.
\v 10 Then¦66238 you¦66238 must¦66238 present the¦66241 Levites¦66241 \add ≈in¦66242 front¦66242 of¦66242\add* Yahweh¦66243 and¦66244 the¦66245 \add ≈Israeli¦66247 men¦66245\add* must¦66244 place¦66244 their¦66250 hands¦66250 on¦66251 them.
\v 11 \add ≈Out of all the Israelis¦66265,\add* Aharon¦66256 must¦66255 present the¦66259 Levites¦66259 as a¦66260 raised offering to¦66261 Yahweh¦66262 \add ≈so¦66266 they¦66266 can serve¦66267 Yahweh¦66271\add* \add with their assigned duties\add*.
\v 12 Then¦66273 the¦66273 Levites¦66273 must¦66274 place¦66274 their¦66277 hands¦66277 on¦66278 the¦66280 bulls¦66280' \add #heads¦66279\add*, and¦66281 one¦66284 must be given as a¦66285 sin¦66285 offering¦66285 and¦66286 the¦66288 other as a¦66289 burnt¦66289 offering¦66289 to¦66290 Yahweh¦66290, to¦66291 make¦66291 the¦66294 Levites¦66294 \add ≈innocent in Yahweh's eyes\add*.
\p
\v 13 “The¦66299 Levites¦66299 must stand¦66296 in¦66300 front¦66300 of¦66300 Aharon¦66301 and¦66302 his¦66303 sons¦66303, then¦66304 they can be offered as a¦66306 raised offering to¦66307 Yahweh¦66307.
\v 14 That's how \add *they'll\add* be \add ≈distinguished¦66309 from¦66313 the¦66314 other Israelis¦66315\add*, and¦66316 then \add *they'll\add* belong to¦66317 me¦66317.
\v 15 Then¦66320 the¦66324 Levites¦66324 will go¦66323 to¦66325 serve¦66325 at the¦66328 \add ≈sacred tent¦66328\add* after¦66320 you've¦66330 purified¦66330 them¦66331 and¦66332 presented them¦66333 as a¦66334 raised offering,
\v 16 because¦66336 they're¦66339 given to¦66340 me¦66340 by all¦66350 the¦66342 Israeli¦66352 people¦66342—I've¦66353 taken¦66353 them for myself in¦66344 place¦66344 of¦66344 their firstborn male sons¦66351,
\v 17 because¦66357 every¦66359 firstborn¦66361 Israeli¦66363 male person¦66364 and¦66365 animal¦66365 belongs to me. I¦66373 set¦66373 them apart¦66373 for myself when I killed¦66367 every¦66368 \add other\add* firstborn¦66370 in¦66371 Egypt¦66372,
\v 18 \add ≈so¦66377\add* I've¦66377 \add now\add* taken¦66377 the¦66380 Levites¦66380 instead of the firstborn¦66384 Israeli¦66386 sons.
\v 19 Then¦66388 I've¦66388 given¦66388 the¦66391 Levites¦66391 out of all the Israelis, to¦66394 Aharon¦66394 and¦66395 his¦66395 sons¦66395 to¦66399 serve¦66399 \add ≈the¦66402 whole country\add* by serving¦66402 in¦66406 the¦66406 \add ≈sacred tent¦66406\add* and¦66408 making¦66408 \add ≈the¦66411 Israelis¦66412 innocent in Yahweh's eyes\add*. That way, a¦66417 \add ≈deadly disease¦66417\add* won't¦66413 strike the¦66415 Israelis¦66416 when¦66418 they approach¦66418 the \add ≈sacred¦66424 tent\add*.”
\p
\v 20 \add ≈So¦66426\add* Mosheh¦66427 and¦66428 Aharon¦66428 and¦66429 all¦66429 the¦66431 \add ≈Israelis¦66434\add* did to¦66435 the Levites¦66435 \add just\add* what Yahweh¦66440 had¦66439 instructed¦66439 Mosheh¦66443.
\v 21 The¦66453 Levites¦66453 purified¦66452 themselves¦66452 and¦66454 washed¦66454 their¦66455 clothes¦66455, and¦66456 Aharon¦66457 offered them¦66458 to¦66460 Yahweh¦66461 as a raised offering, and¦66462 Aharon¦66464 offered a sacrifice to¦66465 \add ≈make¦66462 them¦66465 innocent in Yahweh's eyes\add*.
\v 22 After¦66467 that, the¦66471 Levites¦66471 went¦66470 to¦66472 do their¦66475 \add assigned\add* duties at the¦66476 \add ≈sacred tent¦66476\add* \add ≈working under\add* Aharon¦66479 and¦66480 his¦66481 sons¦66481. \add ≈The Israelis did exactly what Yahweh¦66484 told¦66483 Mosheh¦66487 to do with\add* the¦66490 Levites¦66490.
\p
\v 23 Then¦66496 Yahweh¦66497 told¦66496 Mosheh¦66500,
\v 24 “These are the instructions for the Levites¦66505: from¦66506 the age¦66509 of¦66506 twenty-five, Levite men will¦66511 begin serving¦66512 the work¦66513 in¦66514 the \add ≈sacred tent¦66515\add*
\v 25 until the age¦66520 of¦66518 fifty¦66519 when they must¦66521 retire from¦66522 that work.
\v 26 They may then¦66528 assist¦66528 their fellow Levites¦66541 with guard¦66534 duties¦66535, but¦66536 they can no longer work¦66536 \add directly\add* with the \add ≈sacred tent¦66532\add*.”
\c 9
\s1 The ‘pass-over’ celebration
\rem /s1 The Passover; The Passover at Sinai; The Second Passover
\p
\v 1 Then¦66545 Yahweh¦66546 spoke¦66545 to¦66547 Mosheh¦66549 \add !(Moses¦66549)\add* in¦66550 the¦66550 Sinai¦66552 wilderness¦66550, in¦66553 the¦66554 first¦66559 month¦66558 of¦66555 the¦66556 second year¦66553 \add ≈after they'd left¦66555\add* Egypt¦66557,
\v 2 “The¦66563 \add ≈Israelis¦66563\add* must observe¦66562 ‘pass-over¦66568’ at¦66569 the appointed¦66569 time¦66569.
\v 3 You¦66580 all must¦66580 \add ≈celebrate¦66580\add* it¦66581 on the \add #evening¦66578\add* of the 14th of this¦66576 month¦66575, \add ≈following all¦66583 the instructions¦66585 that you've all¦66586 been given previously\add*.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦66592\add* Mosheh¦66593 \add ≈ordered\add* the¦66596 \add ≈Israelis¦66597\add* to¦66598 \add ≈prepare\add* the¦66599 ‘pass-over¦66599’,
\v 5 and¦66601 they¦66601 \add ≈celebrated\add* it in the Sinai¦66613 wilderness¦66612 \add ≈starting\add* on¦66606 the¦66606 \add #evening¦66611\add* of¦66609 the¦66612 14th of¦66612 that first month, \add ≈following all¦66614 the instructions¦66616 that¦66615 Yahweh¦66617 had¦66616 given\add* Mosheh¦66620.
\p
\v 6 \add ≈However,\add* there were¦66626 some men who¦66628 were¦66629 ‘unclean¦66630’ (because they'd touched a¦66632 dead body) and¦66633 hence they¦66635 weren't able¦66635 to¦66636 \add ≈celebrate¦66636\add* the¦66638 ‘pass-over¦66638’ that day, \add ≈so¦66641\add* they¦66641 \add ≈approached¦66641\add* Mosheh¦66643 and¦66644 Aharon¦66645
\v 7 and¦66649 \add ≈asked¦66649\add* them¦66651, “We¦66653 were¦66654 ‘unclean¦66654’ because¦66657 we'd¦66658 touched a dead body, \add but\add* \add ≈how come¦66660 we're excluded\add* from presenting an offering¦66663 to Yahweh¦66664 \add ≈along with the other Israelis¦66668\add*?”
\p
\v 8 “\add ≈Wait here\add*,” Mosheh¦66672 \add ≈answered¦66670\add*, “and I'll¦66674 \add ask\add* Yahweh¦66678 \add ≈what¦66675 he¦66677 wants you¦66679 all to do\add*.”
\p
\v 9 Then¦66682 Yahweh¦66683 told¦66682 Mosheh¦66686,
\v 10 “Tell¦66689 the¦66692 \add ≈Israelis¦66693 that\add* for¦66708 this and future generations¦66710, if¦66697 a person is¦66699 ‘unclean¦66701’ or \add ≈far from home\add*, then¦66711 they can \add still\add* \add ≈observe¦66711\add* Yahweh's¦66713 ‘pass-over¦66712’.
\v 11 They can \add ≈start\add* it on¦66717 the \add #evening¦66721\add* of the 14th of the¦66716 \em second¦66716\em* month¦66715, and eat¦66728 it¦66723 \add as usual\add* with¦66724 flat¦66726 bread¦66726 and¦66727 bitter¦66727 herbs¦66727.
\v 12 They must not¦66738 break¦66739 \add ≈any of¦66742 the¦66744 lambs bones¦66737\add*, must not leave¦66732 any of¦66744 it until¦66734 the¦66745 morning¦66736, and must¦66746 observe¦66746 it¦66747 \add ≈following all the normal instructions\add*.\x + \xo 9:12: \xt Exo 12:46; Yhn 19:36.\x*
\v 13 \add ≈However,\add* any person¦66749 who¦66750 \add ^isn't ‘unclean’\add* or far away, but¦66754 yet who didn't¦66755 celebrate the¦66760 ‘pass-over¦66760’ \add ≈that first month\add*, must¦66761 be¦66761 \add ≈driven out of¦66764 the¦66767 community\add* and will¦66773 have to bear¦66773 their \add own\add* sin¦66772.
\p
\v 14 If an \add ≈outsider is living¦66779 among you¦66780\add* and¦66782 \add ≈celebrates¦66782\add* the ‘pass-over¦66783’, they must also do it according¦66785 to¦66785 \add ≈all the same instructions\add*—\add ≈there's only one¦66791 way to¦66787 do¦66789 it whether it's\add* you¦66793 all, or a foreigner¦66794, or a native¦66795 of¦66795 the¦66796 land¦66796.
\rem /s1 The journey from Sinai to Edom; The Cloud Above the Tabernacle; The Fiery Cloud; The Cloud and the Fire
\rem /r (Exodus 40.34-38)
\p
\v 15 \add ≈When¦66799 the sacred¦66803 tent¦66803 was dedicated\add*, the¦66805 cloud¦66805 covered¦66804 the¦66808 \add ≈inner room of¦66809 the¦66809 tent¦66809\add*, and¦66811 \add ≈every evening¦66811 it¦66812 would look like¦66816 fire¦66818 above¦66813\add* the¦66815 residence¦66815, until¦66819 morning¦66821 \add came\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈It¦66824 remained like that\add* continually¦66825—the¦66826 cloud¦66826 would cover¦66827 it¦66827 \add during the day\add*, and then¦66828 at night¦66831, it \add ≈would appear¦66828 like\add* fire¦66830.
\v 17 \add ≈Whenever\add* the cloud \add ≈would be lifted up\add* from¦66836 the¦66837 tent¦66837, \add ≈then¦66838 the¦66842 Israelis¦66843\add* would \add ≈leave that place¦66844\add*. \add Then\add* wherever¦66845 the cloud settled¦66846 down¦66846, \add ≈that's where¦66845 the Israelis¦66853 would set¦66841 up camp¦66851\add*,
\v 18 \add so in that way,\add* the \add ≈Israelis¦66861 would leave a place whenever Yahweh¦66865 told them, and would set¦66859 up camp¦66866 whenever he told them\add*. As long as the¦66872 cloud¦66872 stayed above¦66873 the¦66875 residence¦66875, they¦66876 would \add stay\add* camped¦66876 \add in that place\add*.
\v 19 Whenever¦66878 the¦66879 cloud¦66879 remained above¦66880 the¦66882 residence¦66882 for a \add ≈long¦66878 time¦66883\add*, then¦66885 the¦66886 \add ≈Israelis¦66888\add* would \add ≈follow\add* Yahweh's¦66892 \add ≈guidance\add* and¦66893 wouldn't \add ≈pack up camp\add*.
\v 20 Sometimes the¦66899 cloud¦66899 would only remain above¦66902 the¦66904 residence¦66904 for a few days¦66900, in which case they'd \add ≈leave where they'd just camped¦66909, and¦66910 move on¦66910 as Yahweh¦66913 commanded\add*.
\v 21 If the¦66922 cloud¦66922 was¦66927 lifted up¦66927 the¦66928 next morning¦66929, then¦66930 they'd¦66930 \add ≈move on\add*—\add in fact\add* whether day¦66932 or night¦66933 if the cloud was lifted up, then¦66936 they¦66936 would \add ≈move on\add*.
\v 22 Whether it was two¦66940 days¦66940 or¦66941 a¦66943 month¦66943 or¦66944 \add ≈a year\add* that the¦66948 cloud¦66948 stayed above¦66949 the¦66951 residence¦66951, then the¦66955 \add ≈Israeli¦66957\add* camp¦66954 would remain in that place¦66959, until \add eventually\add* \add ≈moving on\add* when¦66960 it¦66960 was¦66960 lifted up¦66960 \add again\add*.
\v 23 \add In that way,\add* \add ≈when Yahweh¦66966 ordered them to camp¦66967, they¦66967 would, and¦66968 when order to move on¦66968, they'd¦66972 do that\add*—thus they¦66977 \add ≈obeyed\add* Yahweh's¦66981 \add ≈instructions to\add* Mosheh¦66984.
\c 10
\s1 The silver trumpets
\rem /s1 The Silver Trumpets
\p
\v 1 Then¦66987 Yahweh¦66988 told¦66987 Mosheh¦66991 \add !(Moses¦66991)\add*,
\v 2 “Make¦66994 two¦66996 hammered¦66999 silver¦66998 trumpets¦66997 for¦67003 yourself¦67003 to use for¦67004 \add ≈assembling the community¦67005\add* and¦67006 for¦67006 \add signalling when it's time\add* to leave the¦67009 \add #camp¦67009\add*.
\v 3 \add ≈When both are sounded, the¦67017 whole¦67015 community¦67017 is to¦67018 assemble in front of\add* you at the¦67020 entrance¦67020 to the¦67021 \add ≈sacred tent¦67021\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈If¦67024 just one¦67026 is sounded,\add* then¦67028 it's \add only\add* the¦67030 leaders¦67030 and heads¦67031 of¦67031 clans who must assemble¦67028.
\v 5 A¦67035 \add ≈single blast¦67035\add* means that¦67039 the¦67038 camps¦67038 on¦67040 the eastern¦67040 side should \add start\add* moving out¦67037.
\v 6 A¦67042 \add ≈double blast¦67042\add* means that¦67047 the¦67046 camps¦67046 on¦67048 the southern¦67048 side should \add start\add* moving out. \add ≈So the blasts will signal them to get going\add*.
\v 7 (To assemble¦67056 the¦67056 community \add as above\add*, \add ≈use long blows¦67057, not¦67058 short blasts¦67057\add*.)
\v 8 The¦67061 priests¦67063 (Aharon's¦67062 descendants) must be the¦67063 ones to blow¦67064 the trumpets¦67065. That is¦67066 a¦67068 \add ≈permanent¦67069\add* regulation¦67068.
\p
\v 9 When¦67072 you¦67074 \add ≈need to defend yourselves against an attacker¦67080\add*, then¦67082 you¦67082 must¦67082 sound an¦67082 alarm¦67082 with the trumpets¦67083, and¦67084 you'll¦67084 all be¦67084 \add ≈noticed\add* by Yahweh¦67087, and¦67089 you'll¦67089 be¦67089 saved¦67089 from¦67090 your¦67090 enemies¦67090.
\p
\v 10 On¦67092 festival \add #days¦67092\add* and¦67094 at¦67094 times of¦67094 celebrations and¦67095 at¦67095 the¦67095 \add #beginning¦67095\add* of¦67095 each new month¦67096, then¦67097 the trumpets¦67098 will¦67097 be blown¦67097 as the burnt¦67100 offerings and¦67101 peace¦67103 offerings¦67103 are¦67104 made as a¦67106 memorial¦67106 for you all towards your god. I¦67109 am¦67110 your god, Yahweh¦67110.
\s1 The Israelis leave Sinai
\rem /s1 The Israelites Leave Sinai; Departure from Sinai; The Israelites Break Camp
\p
\v 11 Then¦67114 on the¦67116 20th of the¦67118 second¦67118 month in that second year¦67115 \add (after leaving Egypt)\add*, the¦67122 cloud¦67122 was lifted up from¦67123 above the¦67124 \add ≈sacred¦67124 tent¦67124\add*
\v 12 and¦67127 the¦67128 \add ≈Israelis¦67128\add* \add ≈started¦67127 moving out¦67131 from¦67132 the¦67132 Sinai¦67133 wilderness as per the pre-arranged order\add*. The¦67135 cloud¦67135 moved to the¦67136 Paran¦67137 wilderness.
\v 13 That was the first time that they¦67139 had moved \add ≈as a result of¦67143 Yahweh¦67144 signalling Mosheh¦67147\add* \add by means of the cloud\add*.
\p
\v 14 Yehudah¦67154 tribe with their banner¦67150 \add ≈was the first¦67155 to¦67156 leave under the¦67161 leadership of¦67161\add* Amminadav's¦67163 son¦67161 Nahshon¦67160.
\v 15 Tsuar's¦67174 son¦67172 Netanel¦67171 led the company from Yissakar¦67170 tribe¦67168,
\v 16 and¦67176 Helon's¦67185 son¦67183 Eliav¦67182 led the company from Zevulun¦67181 tribe¦67179.
