\v 22 Efrayim¦67254 tribe with their¦67255 banner \add ≈was¦67256 next to¦67255 leave under the¦67260 leadership of¦67260\add* Ammihud's¦67262 son¦67260 Elishama¦67259.
\v 23 Pedahtsur's son¦67271 Gamaliel¦67270 led the company from Menashsheh¦67269 tribe¦67267.
\v 24 Gideoni's son¦67284 Avidan led the company from Benyamin¦67282 tribe¦67280.
\p
\v 25 Dan¦67294 tribe with their banner \add ≈was last to leave as the rear guard¦67295 under the leadership of¦67304\add* Ammishaddai's¦67306 son¦67304 Ahiezer¦67303.
\v 26 Okran's¦67318 son¦67316 Pagiel¦67315 led the company from Asher¦67314 tribe¦67312.
\v 27 Eynan's¦67329 son¦67327 Ahira¦67326 led the company from Naftali¦67325 tribe¦67323.
\v 28 That was¦67332 \add ≈the¦67332 order of¦67332 the¦67333 departures of¦67333 the companies of¦67336 the Israeli¦67335 tribes when¦67337 they¦67337\add* set¦67337 off.
\p
\v 29 Then¦67340 Mosheh¦67341 told¦67340 Hovav¦67342 (son¦67343 of¦67343 the Midianite Reuel¦67345 who was Mosheh's¦67348 father-in-law¦67347), “We're¦67351 heading towards the¦67354 place¦67354 that¦67355 Yahweh¦67357 said¦67356 he'd give¦67359 us. Come¦67361 \add ≈and join us¦67362, and¦67363 we'll¦67363 look after you¦67364, because¦67365 Yahweh¦67367 has¦67368 promised to look after\add* Yisrael¦67373.”
\p
\v 30 “\add Thank you but\add* \add ≈no\add*,” \add @Hovav¦67375\add* \add ≈replied¦67375\add*, “I'll¦67378 \add ≈return¦67378\add* to¦67382 my¦67384 land¦67384 and¦67385 to¦67385 my¦67387 relatives¦67387.”
\p
\v 31 “Please¦67393 don't¦67391 leave¦67394 us¦67395,” \add @Mosheh\add* \add ≈insisted\add*, “because¦67396 you're¦67401 \add the one who\add* knows¦67401 about camping¦67402 in¦67403 the wilderness¦67403, and¦67404 you¦67404 \add ≈could be our guide\add*.
\v 32 When¦67408 you¦67411 come¦67411 with¦67412 us¦67412, Yahweh¦67419 \add ≈will¦67418 be blessing us¦67420 so¦67421 we'll¦67421 also bless\add* you¦67422.”
\rem /s1 The People Set Out
\p
\v 33 Then¦67424 they¦67424 \add ≈left¦67424\add* Yahweh's¦67426 mountain \add ≈and travelled for\add* three¦67428 days¦67429, with the¦67430 box¦67430 \add ≈containing\add* Yahweh's¦67433 agreement¦67431 \add ≈being¦67434 carried at the front¦67435\add* to find a¦67441 resting¦67441 place¦67441 for them,
\v 34 and¦67443 Yahweh's¦67444 cloud¦67443 was¦67445 over¦67445 them¦67445 \add each\add* day¦67446 as they set out¦67447 from¦67448 their stop.
\p
\v 35 \add ≈As the¦67457 box¦67457 started¦67456 moving\add*, Mosheh¦67459 would say¦67458, “Yahweh¦67462, \add ≈take action\add* and¦67463 then your¦67464 enemies¦67464 will scatter¦67463, and¦67465 the ones hating¦67466 you¦67466 will flee¦67465 away from¦67467 your¦67467 \add ≈presence\add*.”\x + \xo 10:35: \xt Psa 68:1.\x*
\v 36 Then¦67469 \add at the end of the day\add* when¦67469 it¦67469 came to rest¦67469, he¦67470 would say¦67470, “Yahweh¦67472, return¦67471 \add to\add* the¦67473 \add ≈tens¦67473 of thousands¦67473 of Israelis¦67475\add*.”
\c 11
\s1 Complaints and fire from Yahweh
\rem /s1 The People Complain to Moses; The Place Named Taberah; Fire From the Lord; Complaining in the Desert
\p
\v 1 \add ≈One day,\add* the¦67481 people¦67481 were complaining¦67482 \add about their situation\add* and¦67486 \add ≈when Yahweh¦67487 heard¦67486 them, it¦67486 made him angry¦67489\add* \add ≈so¦67488 he sent a fire¦67488 that burnt¦67490 up the edges of their camp¦67497\add*.
\v 2 The¦67500 people¦67500 cried¦67499 out¦67499 to¦67501 Mosheh¦67503 \add for help\add*, and¦67504 \add *he¦67505\add* prayed¦67504 to¦67506 Yahweh¦67508, and¦67509 the¦67510 fire¦67510 stopped,
\v 3 and¦67512 they named¦67513 that¦67516 place¦67515 Taverah \add (which means ‘burning’)\add* because¦67518 Yahweh's¦67523 fire¦67522 had¦67520 burnt¦67520 among¦67521 them¦67521.
\s1 The choosing of seventy elders
\rem /s1 Quail From the Lord; Moses Chooses Seventy Leaders
\p
\v 4 \add ≈However\add*, there was¦67527 a \add ≈group of stirrers among¦67527 the¦67533 people¦67533\add* that \add ≈badly wanted to have meat and other foods to eat\add*. \add ?≈That spread to all the Israelis¦67534 who wept¦67531 and¦67535 asked¦67535\add*, “Who'll¦67536 give us¦67537 meat to¦67537 eat¦67537?
\v 5 We¦67540 remember¦67540 the¦67543 fish¦67543 that¦67544 we¦67546 ate¦67546 in¦67547 Egypt¦67547 for¦67548 free, \add as well as\add* the¦67550 cucumbers¦67550, melons¦67552, leeks¦67555, onions¦67558, and¦67559 garlic¦67561,
\v 6 \add ≈but¦67563\add* now¦67563 our¦67564 appetite¦67564 \add ≈has shrivelled up because we don't¦67566 see anything¦67567 to eat except¦67568 this ‘stuff’\add*.”
\p
\v 7 (The¦67574 ‘stuff’ \add they ate every day\add* was¦67575 \add a bit\add* like¦67575 coriander¦67577 seed¦67575 \add except kind of clear\add*.\x + \xo 11:7-8: \xt Exo 16:31.\x*
\v 8 \add Each morning\add* the¦67584 people¦67584 went¦67583 around¦67583 gathering¦67585 it, then¦67586 ground¦67586 it with a \add stone\add* mill or¦67588 pounded¦67589 it in¦67590 a mortar¦67590, then¦67591 they¦67591 boiled¦67591 it and¦67593 made¦67593 \add ≈something like bread¦67595 rolls with\add* it¦67596. They tasted¦67597 like¦67598 fresh \add olive\add* oil¦67600.
\v 9 The ‘stuff’ \add actually\add* descended¦67602 on¦67604 the¦67606 camp¦67606 during the night¦67607 with the¦67609 dew¦67603.)\x + \xo 11:9: \xt Exo 16:13-15.\x*
\p
\v 10 Mosheh¦67613 heard¦67612 the¦67616 people¦67616 weeping¦67617 in their \add #tents¦67621\add* (set up by tribe and \add #clan¦67618\add*). \add *He\add* thought it¦67629 was¦67629 wrong, and \add it made\add* Yahweh¦67625 \add ≈very¦67626 angry¦67624\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈So¦67631\add* Mosheh¦67632 \add ≈asked¦67631\add* Yahweh¦67635, “Why¦67636 \add ≈have¦67637 you¦67637 caused¦67637 me, your servant¦67638, to be in¦67644 trouble¦67637\add* \add like this\add*? \add ≈Don't¦67640 you approve of¦67644 me?\add*. \add ≈Why\add* has the¦67648 burden¦67648 of¦67648 all¦67649 this¦67652 people¦67651 group \add landed\add* on¦67653 me¦67653?
\v 12 \add ≈Was it me who\add* conceived¦67656 \add *it\add*? \add ≈Did¦67665 I¦67665 carry¦67670 it¦67670 to the land¦67679 promised¦67681 to¦67682 their ancestors¦67682, like I was a wet-nurse\add*?
\v 13 All¦67688 these people¦67690 come to¦67695 me¦67695 to¦67696 ask¦67696 me to give them meat to eat¦67701. Where¦67684 would¦67686 I get \add enough\add* meat \add to feed all\add* them?
\v 14 I can't¦67703 bear¦67708 \add the load of\add* this¦67714 entire¦67711 people¦67713 group by myself—it's¦67716 too¦67716 heavy¦67716 for¦67717 me¦67717.
\v 15 If¦67719 that's what you're¦67723 doing¦67725 to¦67726 me, please¦67728 kill¦67729 me now if¦67730 I've¦67732 found¦67732 favour¦67733 in¦67734 your¦67734 eyes¦67734. \add ≈Then¦67735 I wouldn't have to suffer like this\add*.”
\rem /s1 Moses Chooses Seventy Leaders; The Seventy Elders
\p
\v 16 Then¦67741 Yahweh¦67742 told¦67741 Mosheh¦67745, “Bring me¦67748 seventy¦67749 of¦67752 Yisrael's¦67752 elders who¦67753 you¦67754 know¦67754 \add ≈are¦67758 good leaders\add*, and take¦67761 them¦67762 to¦67763 the¦67765 \add ≈sacred tent¦67765\add*, and¦67767 \add ≈let them take their positions\add* there¦67768 with¦67769 you¦67769.
\v 17 I'll¦67771 come¦67771 down¦67771 and¦67772 talk¦67772 with¦67773 you¦67773 there¦67774, and¦67775 I'll¦67775 take some¦67776 of¦67776 the¦67778 spirit¦67778 that's¦67779 on¦67780 you¦67780 and¦67781 put¦67781 \add <it\add* on¦67782 them¦67782, and¦67783 then they'll¦67783 carry¦67783 the¦67785 burden¦67785 of¦67785 the¦67786 people¦67786 along with you. Then¦67787 you¦67789 won't¦67787 \add have to\add* carry¦67789 \add <it\add* by yourself.
\v 18 \add ≈Also¦67793,\add* tell the¦67795 people¦67795 that because¦67801 they wept¦67802 in¦67803 \add *my¦67804\add* hearing about¦67803 not having meat to eat like you all did in¦67813 Egypt¦67813, they must \add ≈purify¦67797\add* themselves for¦67798 tomorrow¦67798, because \add *I'll\add* provide meat for you all to eat¦67818.
\v 19 You won't¦67820 \add just\add* have meat for a¦67821 day¦67821 or two¦67825, or for five¦67828, ten¦67831, or twenty¦67834 days¦67835,
\v 20 you have it for a¦67839 \add whole\add* month¦67839 until¦67841 it¦67844 comes¦67844 out¦67844 your¦67845 nostrils¦67845. \add Yes,\add* it'll¦67846 make you¦67847 all nauseous¦67848 because you¦67852 rejected¦67852 Yahweh¦67855 who's¦67856 among¦67857 you, and¦67858 you¦67858 all wept¦67858 \add ≈in¦67859 front¦67859 of¦67859 him¦67859, complaining\add*, ‘Why did¦67863 we¦67863 ever leave Egypt¦67864?’ ”
\p
\v 21 Mosheh¦67867 \add ≈queried\add*, “There's 600,000 \add ≈able to serve in¦67876 the¦67873 army\add* \add plus women and children\add*, yet you say¦67878 that¦67874 you'll give¦67880 them \add all\add* enough meat¦67879 to¦67881 eat¦67882 \add every\add* day¦67884 for month¦67883!
\v 22 \add ≈Even if we killed all the cattle and sheep¦67886, or¦67892 caught all¦67895 the¦67897 fish¦67897 in the¦67898 sea¦67898, that wouldn't be¦67899 enough meat\add* for \add all\add* them.”
\p
\v 23 “\add Do you think that\add* Yahweh's¦67906 \add ≈powerless\add*?” Yahweh¦67911 \add ≈replied¦67905\add*. “\add ≈Soon\add* you'll¦67914 see¦67914 whether or¦67917 not¦67919 my statement will \add ≈come¦67915 true\add*.”
\p
\v 24 \add ≈So¦67921\add* Mosheh¦67922 went¦67921 out¦67921 and¦67923 \add ≈passed on\add* Yahweh's¦67929 \add #message¦67928\add* to¦67924 the¦67926 people¦67926. Then¦67930 he¦67930 gathered¦67930 seventy¦67931 men¦67932 from the¦67933 \add ≈Israeli\add* elders¦67933 and¦67935 stood them¦67936 around¦67937 the¦67938 tent¦67938.
\v 25 Then¦67940 Yahweh¦67941 came¦67940 down in¦67943 the cloud¦67943 and¦67944 spoke¦67944 to¦67945 \add @Mosheh¦67945\add*, and¦67946 he¦67946 took \add ≈some¦67947 of¦67947\add* the¦67949 spirit¦67949 away from him¦67951 and¦67952 put¦67946 it¦67952 on¦67953 those seventy¦67955 elders¦67957. As¦67959 the spirit rested¦67959 on¦67960 them¦67960, they¦67962 prophesied¦67962 \add ≈(but¦67963 they¦67964 never did that¦67950 again)\add*.
\p
\v 26 Two¦67967 of¦67967 the men¦67969 who were listed (named Eldad¦67975 and¦67976 Meydad¦67978), had remained¦67966 in¦67971 the \add main\add* camp (not¦67984 going¦67985 to¦67986 the¦67986 \add sacred\add* tent¦67986), and the¦67981 spirit¦67981 had \add also\add* rested¦67979 on¦67980 them¦67980 and they¦67987 prophesied¦67987 in¦67988 the camp¦67988.
\v 27 A young¦67991 man¦67991 ran¦67990 to¦67993 Mosheh¦67993 and¦67994 told¦67994 him that Eldad¦67995 and¦67996 Meydad¦67996 were¦67997 prophesying¦67997 \add there\add* in¦67998 the camp¦67998.
\p
\v 28 Then¦68000 Nun's¦68004 son¦68002 Yehoshua¦68001 (who had helped Mosheh¦68006 since his¦68007 youth¦68007) \add ≈responded¦68008\add*, “My¦68009 master¦68009 Mosheh¦68010, stop¦68011 them¦68011 \add from that\add*.”
\p
\v 29 \add ≈But¦68013\add* Mosheh¦68015 replied¦68013, “Are¦68017 you¦68017 being jealous¦68016 \add ≈on my behalf\add*? \add ≈I'd be happy if\add* Yahweh¦68029 would¦68028 put¦68028 his¦68032 spirit¦68032 on¦68033 \em all¦68021\em* the¦68023 people¦68023 and \add ≈make them¦68033 into\add* prophets¦68025.”
\v 30 Then¦68035 Mosheh¦68036 and¦68041 the¦68041 elders¦68041 \add ≈went back to their tents\add*.
\s1 Yahweh sends quails for meat
