\p
\v 27 “\add ≈Now\add* if¦70066 a¦70068 single¦70069 person¦70068 disobeys by¦70071 mistake, then¦70072 that person must¦70072 present a¦70073 one-year-old female¦70073 goat¦70073 as a¦70077 sin¦70077 offering¦70077,
\v 28 and¦70079 the¦70080 priest¦70080 will¦70079 make¦70079 atonement¦70079 for that¦70084 person. \add In that way,\add* the¦70087 one making a mistake in¦70087 front¦70087 of¦70087 Yahweh¦70088 will¦70091 be¦70091 forgiven¦70091.
\v 29 \add Both\add* \add ≈native-born¦70094 Israelis¦70096\add* and¦70097 foreigners¦70097 living¦70098 among¦70099 them¦70099 must \add all\add* \add ≈follow the same instructions¦70100 after\add* making a¦70100 mistake.
\v 30 \add ≈However,\add* any person¦70107 who¦70108 \add ≈disobeys defiantly\add*, whether native-born¦70116 or foreigner, they are slandering Yahweh¦70122 and¦70125 that¦70127 person¦70129 must be \add ≈driven out of¦70129 the community\add*
\v 31 because¦70131 they've despised¦70135 Yahweh's¦70134 message¦70132 and¦70136 disobeyed his¦70138 instructions¦70138. That¦70144 person must¦70142 be¦70142 \add ≈completely\add* cut¦70142 off¦70142 and their guilt¦70145 \add remains\add* on¦70146 them.
