\v 12 Then¦70521 Mosheh¦70522 \add ≈summoned¦70523\add* Eliav's¦70527 sons¦70526 Datan¦70524 and¦70525 Aviram¦70525 \add ≈but¦70528 they¦70528 refused\add*, “We¦70530 won't¦70529 come¦70530.
\v 13 \add ^Isn't it enough\add* that¦70533 you¦70534 brought¦70534 us¦70534 \em out\em* of a¦70535 land¦70535 flowing¦70536 with milk¦70537 and¦70538 honey¦70538, to¦70539 kill¦70539 us¦70539 \add here\add* in¦70540 the wilderness¦70540, without also¦70545 making¦70543 yourself¦70543 the ruler¦70543 over¦70544 us¦70544?
\v 14 \add ≈What's more\add*, you didn't¦70550 bring¦70557 us into¦70551 a¦70553 land¦70553 flowing¦70554 with milk¦70555 and¦70556 honey¦70556 or give¦70558 us¦70560 an¦70561 inheritance¦70561 of¦70561 land and¦70563 \add #vineyards¦70563\add*. Will¦70567 you¦70567 gouge¦70567 out¦70567 the¦70564 eyes¦70564 of¦70564 those¦70566 \add @Kanaanites\add* \add so that we can defeat them\add*? \add No,\add* we¦70569 won't come¦70569.”
\p
