\v 27 \add ≈So¦70771\add* \add @the¦70771 rest¦70771 of¦70771 the¦70771 Israelis¦70771\add* \add ≈kept back\add* from¦70772 the¦70773 residences of¦70773 Korah¦70775, Datan¦70777, and¦70778 Aviram¦70778. \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* Datan¦70780 and¦70781 Aviram¦70781 had come¦70782 out¦70782 of¦70785 their¦70785 tents¦70785, and were standing¦70783 at the¦70784 \add #entrances¦70784\add* with their¦70786 wives¦70786 and¦70787 children¦70787.
\p
\v 28 Then¦70790 Mosheh¦70791 said¦70790, “This¦70792 is how \add you'll all\add* known¦70793 that¦70794 \add it was\add* Yahweh¦70796 \add ≈who selected me¦70797 for¦70798 this role\add*—it's¦70790 \add never\add* \add ≈been something that¦70804 I aspired to\add*:
\v 29 If¦70809 all¦70812 these¦70816 men¦70814 \add ≈die¦70815 a natural death¦70811 like¦70811 most people¦70814\add*, then¦70817 Yahweh¦70824 didn't¦70823 \add ≈choose\add* me¦70825,
\v 30 \add ≈but¦70827\add* if¦70827 Yahweh¦70831 \add ≈does something new\add* and¦70832 the¦70833 ground¦70833 opens¦70832 its¦70836 mouth¦70836 and¦70837 swallows¦70837 them¦70838 and their homes and tents and \add ≈all¦70841 their possessions\add*, and¦70845 if they¦70845 then go¦70845 down¦70845 alive¦70846 into¦70847 \add ≈their grave\add*, then¦70848 you'll¦70848 all know¦70848 that it was because these¦70852 men¦70851 rejected¦70850 Yahweh¦70855.”
\p
\v 31 \add ≈As soon as Mosheh had finished¦70858 speaking¦70859\add*, the ground¦70866 below \add @those men\add* split¦70865 open¦70865
\v 32 and¦70870 the¦70871 earth¦70871 opened¦70870 its¦70874 mouth¦70874 and¦70875 swallowed¦70875 them¦70876 and¦70877 their¦70879 homes¦70879 and¦70880 every¦70881 man¦70883 who¦70884 \add ≈backed\add* Korah¦70885 along with all¦70887 \add &their¦70889\add* property¦70889.
\v 33 They¦70891 went¦70891 down¦70891 alive¦70897 to¦70898 \add ≈their grave\add*, along with everything they owned, and¦70899 then the¦70901 ground¦70901 covered¦70899 over¦70900 them¦70900 and¦70902 they¦70902 \add ≈vanished\add* from¦70903 the¦70904 \add ≈community\add*.
\v 34 All¦70906 the people who were¦70910 around¦70910 them¦70910 fled¦70911 \add away\add* \add ≈screaming because¦70913 they¦70914 were afraid of getting swallowed¦70917 by the¦70918 earth¦70918 as well\add*.
\p
\v 35 Then¦70920 Yahweh¦70923 \add ≈sent\add* fire¦70920 that consumed¦70924 the¦70926 250 men¦70928 who¦70929 were¦70929 presenting¦70929 incense¦70930.
\s1 The incense burners
