\v 6 \add ≈Now listen\add*, I've¦71558 taken¦71558 your¦71561 brothers¦71561 the¦71562 Levites¦71562 \add ≈out from¦71563 the rest of the Israelis¦71565\add* as a¦71567 gift¦71567 for¦71569 you—they're¦71568 given to¦71570 \add ≈do the¦71573 duties\add* at the¦71574 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦71574.
\v 7 \add ≈However,\add* it's you¦71577 and¦71578 your¦71578 sons¦71578 who \add ≈are the¦71586 priests\add* who must¦71590 serve¦71590 for things to do with the¦71587 altar¦71587 and¦71588 inside¦71588 the curtain¦71589. Your priesthood is a¦71592 gift¦71592 of¦71596 service¦71591, and¦71597 any¦71584 \add ≈outsider¦71597\add* who approaches¦71598 must¦71599 be¦71599 executed¦71599.”
