\v 6 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* the¦72194 priest¦72194 must take¦72193 some cedar¦72196 wood¦72195, hyssop¦72197, and¦72198 scarlet wool, and¦72200 throw¦72200 them¦72200 into¦72201 \add the fire\add* where the cow is burning¦72204.
\v 7 Then¦72207 the¦72209 priest¦72209 must¦72210 wash¦72210 his¦72211 clothes¦72208 and¦72213 bathe. After¦72213 that, he¦72214 can return¦72214 to¦72215 the¦72217 camp¦72217, \add ≈but¦72218\add* \add *he'll\add* be¦72218 ‘unclean¦72218’ until¦72220 that evening¦72222.
\v 8 The¦72224 \add man\add* who¦72224 burnt¦72224 \add @the cow\add* must¦72226 \add also\add* wash¦72226 his¦72227 clothes¦72227 and¦72229 bathe, and¦72232 he¦72232 will¦72232 \add also\add* be¦72232 ‘unclean¦72232’ until¦72233 that evening¦72235.
\v 9 A¦72239 ‘clean’ man¦72239 must collect¦72237 the¦72242 cow's ashes¦72242 and¦72244 place them¦72244 in¦72247 a¦72247 \add ≈sacred\add* place¦72247 outside¦72245 the camp¦72246 where they can be used for¦72250 water¦72255 for purification for the \add ≈Israelis¦72253\add* to¦72255 purify from \add ≈disobedience\add*.
