\v 11 “ ‘\add #All¦72284 those\add* who¦72282 touch¦72282 a¦72283 dead¦72283, human body¦72283 will¦72288 be¦72288 ‘unclean¦72288’ for seven¦72289 days¦72290.
\v 12 On the third day, they must purify themselves, and¦72298 then they'll be ‘clean’ on¦72298 the¦72299 seventh¦72299 day. (If¦72301 they don't¦72303 purify¦72304 themselves, they'll won't become ‘clean’ on¦72307 that seventh day—
\v 13 if they've touched¦72314 a¦72315 dead¦72315, human¦72317 body¦72315 and¦72321 don't¦72321 purify¦72322 themselves, that would defile Yahweh's¦72326 residence, and¦72328 \add so\add* they must¦72328 be¦72328 \add ?≈permanently removed from¦72331 the camp\add*. If¦72332 the¦72333 purifying water¦72333 wasn't sprinkled¦72337 on¦72338 them, that ‘uncleanness¦72339’ will¦72340 remain on them.)
\p
\v 14 “ ‘This¦72345 is¦72346 the¦72346 regulation if¦72348 a person dies¦72350 in¦72351 a¦72351 tent¦72351: Everyone¦72354 who¦72354 was in¦72355 the¦72357 tent¦72357, and¦72358 everyone¦72358 that¦72360 enters \add afterwards\add*, will¦72362 all¦72358 be¦72362 ‘unclean¦72362’ for seven¦72363 days¦72364,
\v 15 and¦72366 every¦72366 container¦72367 that¦72369 doesn't have its lid on¦72374 becomes ‘unclean¦72375’.
\v 16 \add ≈Out in\add* the¦72385 countryside¦72385, who¦72379 touches¦72381 the¦72384 corpse of¦72384 someone killed¦72386 in¦72386 a¦72388 fight, or¦72389 any¦72378 dead¦72390 human¦72394 body¦72390 or¦72391 bone¦72393 or¦72395 grave¦72396, will¦72397 be¦72397 ‘unclean¦72397’ for seven¦72398 days¦72399.
