\p
\v 1 \add ≈By now,\add* Bileam¦74897 \add ≈had realised¦74896\add* that¦74898 Yahweh¦74901 wanted to¦74902 bless¦74902 \add ≈the Israelis¦74905\add*, \add ≈so¦74906\add* he¦74908 didn't¦74906 \add ≈use his usual divinations\add* \add ≈but¦74914 instead, he¦74914 just looked towards\add* the¦74917 wilderness¦74917.
\v 2 \add *He¦74921\add* \add ≈looked up¦74920\add* and¦74925 saw¦74925 Yisrael¦74928 \add ≈in their tents laid out by tribe¦74930\add*. Then¦74931 God's¦74934 spirit¦74933 came onto him,
\v 3 and¦74936 he¦74936 \add ≈made his¦74937 pronouncement\add*,
\q1 “\add This is\add* the¦74939 declaration¦74939 of¦74939 Bileam¦74940, son¦74941 of¦74942 Beor¦74942—
\q1 ≈the¦74943 utterance¦74943 of¦74943 a man¦74944 whose \add #eyes¦74946\add* are open¦74945.
\q1
\v 4 The¦74948 declaration¦74948 of¦74948 someone¦74949 who¦74949 heard¦74949 God's¦74952 \add #message¦74950\add*,
\q1 ≈someone who¦74953 sees¦74956 the¦74954 all-powerful¦74955 one's¦74949 vision¦74954,
