\v 6 ⇔\add ≈Just then¦75329, unbelievably,\add* an \add ≈Israeli¦75332\add* man¦75330 \add ≈came¦75333 past\add* Mosheh¦75342 and¦75343 \add ≈all¦75344 the people¦75347\add* who were \add there outside\add* the \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦75353 weeping¦75351, and he was bringing¦75334 a Midyanite¦75340 woman \add ≈with him\add*.
\v 7 \add ≈When¦75356\add* Pinehas (son¦75358 of¦75358 Eleazar¦75360, son¦75361 of¦75361 Aharon¦75363) saw¦75356 \add <that\add*, he¦75365 \add ≈came out\add* from¦75366 among¦75366 the¦75367 \add ≈gathered people¦75367\add*, grabbed¦75368 a¦75369 spear¦75369,
\v 8 and¦75372 followed the¦75374 \add ≈Israeli\add* man¦75374 into¦75377 \add &his¦75379\add* tent¦75379. He¦75380 \add ≈plunged\add* the spear through¦75380 the two of¦75383 them¦75383—right through the¦75385 man¦75385 and¦75387 the¦75389 woman's¦75389 belly¦75392, and¦75393 \add thus\add*, stopped¦75393 the¦75394 \add ≈deadly disease¦75394\add* \add that had started\add* against the¦75396 \add ≈Israelis¦75397\add*.
\v 9 \add ≈However,\add*, twenty-four thousand¦75404 people had \add already\add* died¦75400 from that plague¦75401.
\p
\v 10 Then¦75407 Yahweh¦75408 spoke¦75407 to¦75409 Mosheh¦75411,
\v 11 “Aharon's¦75420 grandson Pinehas has¦75422 \add ≈deflected my¦75425 anger¦75425\add* from¦75426 the¦75427 \add ≈Israelis¦75429\add* by \add ≈demonstrating my¦75433 seriousness about their behaviour\add*, \add ≈so¦75435 now\add* in my zeal, I¦75437 won't¦75435 \add ≈eliminate the¦75440 Israelis¦75442\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈So¦75445\add* tell¦75446 him¦75449 that I'm \add ≈making\add* a peace¦75453 agreement¦75452 with him.
\v 13 It's¦75455 an agreement¦75459 that¦75463 gives him¦75456 and¦75457 his \add ≈descendants¦75457\add* \add ≈the rights to be priests¦75460\add* because¦75462 he¦75464 was¦75464 zealous¦75464 \add ≈on his god's¦75465 behalf\add* and¦75466 he¦75466 \add ≈worked towards removing the guilt\add* of the \add ≈people¦75469\add*.”
