\p
\v 1 Then¦76379 the¦76380 daughters¦76380 of¦76380 Tselofehad¦76381 (son¦76382 of¦76382 Hefer¦76384, son¦76385 of¦76385 Gilead¦76387, son¦76388 of¦76388 Makir¦76390, son¦76391 of¦76391 Menashsheh) approached¦76379. \add *Their\add* names¦76400 were Mahlah¦76402, Noah¦76403, Hoglah¦76404, Milkah¦76405, and¦76406 Tirtsah¦76406.
\v 2 They¦76408 stood¦76408 \add ≈in¦76409 front¦76409 of¦76409\add* Mosheh¦76410 and¦76411 the¦76413 priest¦76413 Eleazar¦76412 and¦76414 all¦76416 the¦76415 leaders¦76415 and¦76416 the¦76418 people¦76418 \add there\add* at the¦76419 entrance¦76419 to the¦76420 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦76420, \add and\add* \add ≈asked¦76423\add*,
\v 3 “Our¦76425 father¦76425 died¦76426 in¦76427 the wilderness¦76427, \add ≈although\add* he wasn't \add ≈part of the group who joined Korah¦76440 to rebel\add* against Yahweh¦76437—it was \add ≈for¦76441 his¦76443 own¦76443 personal disobedience\add* that¦76434 he¦76444 died¦76444. He didn't have any sons¦76445
\v 4 \add but\add* why should his family name¦76453 disappear from¦76456 our clan¦76457 \add just\add* because¦76458 he had no \add #sons¦76461\add*? \add So\add* give¦76462 us \add ≈some land like\add* our¦76468 father's¦76468 relatives¦76467 will be getting.”
\p
\v 5 \add ≈So¦76470\add* Mosheh¦76471 took¦76470 their case¦76474 to¦76476 Yahweh¦76477
\v 6 and¦76480 \add *he\add* \add ≈responded\add*,
\v 7 “It's right¦76487 what Tselofehad's¦76489 daughters¦76488 are¦76490 saying¦76490. You¦76492 must¦76492 give¦76492 them¦76493 \add ≈some land like their¦76498 father's¦76498 relatives¦76497 will¦76499 be getting\add*. \add ≈Give them whatever would have been given to their¦76503 father¦76503 as his\add* inheritance.
\v 8 \add ≈Also¦76506,\add* tell the¦76508 \add ≈people¦76508\add* that if¦76513 a¦76512 man¦76512 dies¦76515 \add ≈without sons¦76516\add*, then¦76519 his¦76522 inheritance¦76522 should go¦76519 to¦76523 his¦76523 daughter¦76523(s).
\v 9 If¦76525 he had no \add ≈children\add*, then \add ≈it¦76528 should go\add* to¦76534 his¦76534 brothers¦76534,
\v 10 and¦76537 if¦76537 he has no brothers¦76541, then¦76542 \add ≈it should go\add* to¦76546 his¦76547 father's¦76547 brothers.
\v 11 \add ≈However,\add* if¦76549 his¦76553 father¦76553 had no brothers¦76552, then¦76554 the inheritance¦76557 \add ≈should go to¦76558 his¦76558 nearest¦76559 blood-relative to¦76560 become his¦76561 possession¦76562\add*. That will¦76564 \add ≈become¦76564 a¦76567 permanent regulation¦76567\add* for¦76565 Yisrael¦76566, just¦76569 as¦76569 Yahweh¦76571 has¦76570 commanded¦76570.”
