\p
\v 1 ⇔\add ≈While\add* they were there on the Moav¦80542 plains¦80541 beside the¦80545 Yarden¦80545 \add river\add*, Yahweh¦80537 told¦80536 Mosheh¦80540 \add !(Moses¦80540)\add*.\x + \xo 35:1-8: \xt Josh 21:1-42.\x*
\v 2 “Tell the¦80552 \add Israelis\add* that out of¦80552 the land¦80560 that they'll \add ≈own¦80557\add*, they¦80554 must¦80554 give¦80554 the Levites¦80555 cities¦80558 for them to¦80559 live¦80559 in¦80559, \add ≈as well as\add* some¦80556 pastureland¦80560 around¦80562 \add &those\add* cities.
\v 3 The¦80567 cities¦80567 will be for¦80568 them¦80568 to¦80569 live¦80569 in¦80569, and¦80570 that pastureland¦80570 will¦80571 be¦80571 for¦80572 their¦80572 herds¦80572 and¦80573 their¦80573 flocks, and¦80574 for¦80574 their¦80575 other \add #animals¦80575\add*.
\v 4 The¦80577 pastureland¦80577 must¦80580 extend out half a kilometre around¦80587 the¦80582 \add #walls¦80582\add* of¦80582 the¦80583 Levites¦80581 cities¦80583.
\v 5 Then going out a kilometre \add ≈in¦80620 each compass direction\add*, that¦80621 will¦80622 also be their land¦80624.\f + \fr 35:5 \ft It's not exactly clear what different activities would occur in these two rings of land, but remember that as much food as possible and animals would have to be brought into the city as soon as the residents received news of an approaching army.\f*
\rem /s1 Cities of Refuge
\v 6 The¦80628 Levites¦80631 \add ≈must¦80630 be given¦80630 forty-two cities to¦80631 live in, plus\add* you all must¦80632 \add ≈designate\add* six¦80633 refuge cities so that¦80637 if someone accidentally kills¦80641 another, they can flee¦80639 to¦80640 the refuge city¦80646.
\v 7 \add ≈That¦80651 would make a total¦80648 of¦80648\add* forty-eight cities¦80650, plus their¦80660 pasturelands¦80660, to be given¦80652 to¦80653 the Levites¦80653.
\v 8 The¦80662 larger tribes must¦80664 give¦80664 more cities than the smaller¦80673 tribes, according¦80676 to¦80676 the¦80676 area that¦80678 they¦80679 inherit¦80679.”
\s1 The refuge cities
\rem /s1 Cities of Refuge; The Cities of Refuge
