\p
\v 9 Then¦80685 Yahweh¦80686 told¦80685 Mosheh¦80689,\x + \xo 35:9-28: \xt Deu 19:2-4; Josh 20:1-9.\x*
\v 10 “Tell¦80692 the¦80695 \add ≈Israelis¦80696\add* that when¦80697 you cross¦80701 the¦80704 Yarden¦80704 \add river\add* \add ≈to enter\add* Kanaan¦80706,
\v 11 you¦80708 all must¦80708 choose some cities to become ‘refuge¦80712 cities’ \add so that\add* if someone \add ≈accidentally¦80721\add* kills another person¦80720, they¦80713 can flee¦80715 there.
\v 12 The¦80725 cities¦80725 will¦80723 be¦80723 places to¦80724 stay safe from¦80727 \add ≈being avenged¦80727\add* \add by the relatives\add* until¦80731 the¦80730 killer¦80730 can \add ≈be formally tried\add*.
\v 13 You¦80740 all must¦80740 \add ≈allocate\add* six¦80741 refuge¦80744 cities—
\v 14 three¦80750 on the eastern side¦80753 of¦80754 the Yarden¦80754, and¦80755 there on the western side in¦80759 Kanann.
\v 15 Both \add ≈Israelis¦80766\add* and¦80767 \add ≈foreigners¦80767 living in¦80775 the country\add* can flee¦80776 to¦80777 \add any of\add* those¦80774 six¦80771 cities¦80773—anyone¦80780 who¦80780 kills¦80780 \add another\add* person¦80782 by¦80783 accident¦80783.
\rem /s1 Concerning Murder and Blood Revenge
\p
\v 16 “However, if¦80785 someone strikes¦80790 \add @another¦80790 person¦80790\add* with \add ≈a metal object¦80787\add* and¦80791 they die¦80791, then that person is¦80792 a¦80792 murderer¦80792, and murderers must¦80795 be¦80795 \add ≈executed¦80795\add*.
\v 17 \add ≈Similarly,\add* anyone who strikes¦80805 \add @another person\add* when¦80798 holding a¦80799 \add rock or\add* stone¦80799, then that¦80801 person is¦80807 a¦80807 murderer¦80807, and murderers must¦80810 be¦80810 \add ≈executed¦80810\add*.
\v 18 \add ≈Again,\add* if someone¦80820 strikes¦80822 \add @another person\add* with¦80814 a piece of¦80814 wood¦80815, then that¦80818 person is¦80824 a¦80824 murderer¦80824, and murderers must¦80827 be¦80827 \add ≈executed¦80827\add*.
\v 19 The¦80830 \add relative who\add* is avenging¦80830 the¦80831 \add spilt\add* blood¦80831 must¦80833 \add ≈execute¦80833 the¦80836 murderer¦80836 as soon as he finds them\add*.
\p
\v 20 “If¦80843 someone pushes¦80846 \add @another person\add* in¦80845 hatred¦80845, or¦80847 lies¦80851 in¦80851 wait¦80851 and¦80852 then throws¦80849 something at them,
\v 21 or¦80854 angrily strikes¦80856 them with¦80857 their hand¦80857, and¦80858 then they die¦80859, \add ≈it must¦80861 be¦80861 regarded as murder,\add* and when¦80871 the¦80865 avenger¦80865 of¦80865 \add &their¦80866\add* blood¦80866 finds the¦80870 murderer¦80870, he must \add ≈execute\add* them.
\p
\v 22 “\add ≈But¦80875\add* if¦80875 someone pushes¦80881 \add @another¦80881 person¦80881\add* without any¦80886 hateful \add intent\add*, or¦80882 throws¦80884 something at them without lying¦80890 in¦80890 wait¦80890,
\v 23 or¦80892 drops a rock¦80895 without \add ≈noticing\add* someone¦80898, and they die¦80904 \add ≈but¦80905\add* they weren't \add @that¦80905 person's¦80905\add* enemy¦80908 and¦80910 no harm¦80912 was intended,
\v 24 then¦80914 the¦80915 community¦80915 must judge¦80914 between¦80916 the¦80917 \add ≈one¦80917 who¦80917 killed¦80917\add* and¦80918 the¦80919 avenger¦80919 \add ≈of¦80919 the dead person\add*, in accordance with these¦80923 regulations.
\v 25 \add If the one who killed is declared innocent\add*, then¦80925 the¦80926 community¦80926 must rescue¦80925 them from¦80930 the¦80931 avenger¦80931 and¦80933 return¦80933 them to¦80936 the¦80938 refuge¦80939 city¦80938 that they'd fled¦80942 to¦80943, and¦80944 \add ≈that accidental killer¦80929\add* must¦80944 live¦80944 there until¦80946 after the¦80948 death¦80948 of¦80948 the¦80949 high priest¦80949 (who¦80951 had¦80953 been anointed¦80953 with¦80955 \add ≈sacred¦80956\add* oil¦80955).
\v 26 \add ≈However,\add* if¦80958 they then¦80958 ever¦80960 left the refuge¦80967 city¦80966 that they'd fled¦80969 to¦80970,
\v 27 and¦80972 the¦80974 avenger¦80974 found¦80972 them outside¦80976 the¦80978 city¦80978 boundary¦80977, then¦80980 \add ≈that relative of¦80981 the dead person\add* is¦80986 permitted to¦80987 kill¦80980 that person and won't¦80986 be accountable for their blood¦80988.
\v 28 \add That's\add* because¦80990 the¦80991 \add ≈one who killed\add* must¦80993 remain¦80993 in that city¦80991 until¦80994 the¦80996 death¦80996 of¦80996 the high priest—they can only return¦81003 to \add ≈their family home\add* after¦80999 the¦81000 high priest's death.
\v 29 You¦81012 all¦81016 must¦81010 \add follow\add* these¦81011 \add #regulations¦81013\add* through the generations¦81015 no matter where you live¦81017.
\p
\v 30 “\add If\add* someone¦81021 murders \add another\add* person¦81023, they're to¦81024 be executed if there's evidence from witnesses¦81025 (\add plural,\add* not just one¦81026 witness¦81030).
\v 31 That sentence \add ≈can't¦81038 be changed to a fine and/or a payment to¦81048 the deceased's family\add*—\add @the¦81052 murderer¦81052\add* \em must¦81052\em* be¦81052 executed¦81052.
\v 32 \add ≈Similarly for the accidental killer who fled¦81058 to a¦81057 refuge¦81062 city¦81061\add*, they can't¦81054 \add ≈elect to pay a fine and/or pay compensation\add* in order to¦81059 be able to¦81063 return¦81063 \add ≈home\add* before the high priest's¦81069 death¦81068.
\v 33 You¦81073 mustn't profane the¦81076 land¦81076 that¦81077 you're¦81078 all going to \add by tolerating murder\add*, because¦81080 \add human\add* blood¦81081 pollutes¦81083 the¦81086 ground¦81086, and¦81087 you all can't \add ≈restore the land¦81087 with any sacrifice\add*—only by¦81099 the¦81099 blood¦81099 of¦81099 the¦81100 one¦81100 who¦81100 shed¦81100 \add someone else's\add* blood.
\v 34 You¦81103 mustn't profane the¦81106 land¦81106 that¦81107 you'll¦81108 all be¦81109 living¦81109 in¦81110 because¦81115 I'll¦81112 also¦81102 be¦81113 living¦81113 in it, as I¦81116 will live¦81118 among¦81114 \add you\add* \add ≈Israelis¦81121\add*.”
\c 36
\s1 Women inheriting property
