\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* the leaders of the Gilead¦81130 clans¦81137 (\add ≡Gilead was\add* the¦81131 son¦81131 of¦81131 Makir¦81133, son¦81134 of¦81134 Menashsheh¦81136, one of¦81138 Yosef's¦81139 sons) approached¦81124 Mosheh¦81142 and¦81143 the¦81144 \add ≈Israeli¦81148\add* leaders¦81144
\v 2 and¦81150 said¦81150, “Yahweh¦81155 commanded¦81154 my master to¦81156 \add ≈distribute\add* the¦81159 land¦81159 by¦81161 lot¦81161 as an inheritance \add ≈for the¦81162 people¦81162\add*, and¦81164 my master was¦81165 \add also\add* commanded¦81165 by¦81166 Yahweh¦81166 to¦81167 give¦81167 our¦81172 brother¦81172 Tselofehad's¦81171 inheritance to¦81173 his¦81173 daughters¦81173.\x + \xo 36:2: \xt Num 27:7.\x*
\v 3 \add ≈However, if\add* they¦81175 \add ended up\add* \add ≈being¦81175 married by men¦81179 from¦81177 other\add* tribes¦81178, then their inheritance would¦81183 \add ≈pass from¦81185 our¦81186 tribe¦81190 to¦81193 their husbands' tribes, so¦81194 we'd end up with less land as our¦81195 tribal\add* inheritance¦81195.
\v 4 Then when Yisrael¦81203 celebrates the¦81201 Jubilee¦81201 \add Year\add*, then¦81204 that¦81209 inheritance will¦81204 be¦81204 added¦81204 to¦81206 the¦81207 inheritance¦81207 of¦81207 \add @their husbands'\add* tribes¦81208, and¦81212 be deducted from¦81212 the¦81212 inheritance¦81212 of¦81212 our¦81214 \add ≈ancestral¦81214\add* tribe.”
\p
\v 5 Then¦81218 Mosheh¦81219 \add ≈gave a ruling\add* to the \add ≈Israelis¦81223\add* \add ≈in accordance with what Yahweh¦81227 had told¦81228 him\add*, “These \add ≈Yosefite men¦81222\add* are¦81234 correct¦81229.
\v 6 Yahweh's¦81241 \add ≈command¦81240\add* to Tselofehad's¦81243 daughters¦81242 is that¦81238 \add ≈each of you may marry whoever you want as long as it's someone from your own¦81246\add* tribe¦81251.
\v 7 That way, land \add ≈in Yisrael\add* won't¦81256 \add ≈move¦81258\add* from¦81262 tribe¦81262 to¦81263 tribe¦81265, because¦81266 \add ≈it will always stay as part of\add* the inheritance \add ≈given to that\add* tribe¦81269.
\v 8 \add ≈Any woman¦81288 who¦81278 inherits¦81279 land can only marry someone¦81283 from¦81280 her¦81286 own\add* tribe¦81285, so¦81289 that¦81289 the¦81291 people¦81291 will \add always\add* \add ≈retain ownership of¦81291 their tribal\add* inheritance¦81294.
\v 9 \add &That¦81300\add* inheritance¦81300 mustn't pass¦81299 from¦81301 tribe¦81301 to¦81302 tribe¦81302, but each \add ≈Israeli¦81311\add* tribe¦81309 must¦81308 keep hold¦81308 of¦81310 its inheritance.”
\p
\v 10 ⇔So¦81319 Tselofehad's¦81322 daughters¦81321 obeyed what Yahweh¦81315 had¦81314 told¦81314 Mosheh¦81318,
\v 11 and¦81324 the¦81330 \add five\add* daughters¦81330 (Mahlah¦81325, Tirtsah¦81326, Hoglah¦81327, Milkah¦81328, and¦81329 Noah¦81329) married their¦81333 \add ≈cousins on their¦81333 father's side\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈The men they married\add* were from¦81336 the Menashsheh¦81339 tribe (Yosef's¦81342 son¦81340), so \add ≈their land continued to belong to their¦81346 father's¦81351 family and¦81345\add* tribe¦81349.
\p
\v 13 \add ≈All the above\add* were¦81354 the¦81354 commands¦81354 and¦81355 regulations that¦81356 Yahweh¦81358 ordered¦81357 Mosheh¦81361 to¦81362 tell the¦81364 \add ≈Israelis¦81365\add*, \add while they were camped\add* on the¦81366 Moav¦81367 plains¦81366 beside the¦81369 Yarden¦81369 \add river\add* \add ≈opposite\add* Yeriho¦81370 \add !(Jericho¦81370)\add*.
